                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5509: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-11T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 11,
                                1924—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 11—9:14
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>339. My 334, September 8, 5 p.m. Senior consul Shanghai reports defense
                    commissioner on the one side and Nanking admiral on the other have both agreed
                    to the neutralization of the Whangpoo River and to the revocation of the
                    regulations regarding navigation of the lower Yangtze and of the Whangpoo.</p>
                <p>This if true is very satisfactory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
